      "text": "Step 4: Substitute \\(x = \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\) into the equation. Note that \\(\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\), so \\((\\sin \\frac{\\pi}{2})^7 = 1^7 = 1\\). Also, \\(\\sin\\left(7 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{7\\pi}{2}\\right) = -1\\), \\(\\sin\\left(5 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{5\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\), \\(\\sin\\left(3 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = \\sin\\left(\\frac{3\\pi}{2}\\right) = -1\\), and \\(\\sin\\left(\\frac{\\pi}{2}\\right) = 1\\). Therefore, the equation becomes:\n\\[1 = a(-1) + b(1) + c(-1) + d(1).\\]\nThis simplifies to:\n\\[1 = -a + b - c + d.\\]",
